// minerpg: Jobs+ integration (the parts Jobs+/Arc data files can't express).
// Design and numbers: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-30-minerpg-jobs-integration-design.md,
// "Implementation notes". The data half (crafting/brewing gates, crafting XP bonuses, rune and
// potion charm XP, level milestones) is generated by pack/tools/gen_jobs.py into the
// minerpg_jobs datapack (config/originpacks/minerpg_jobs/).
//
// This script:
//   - /minerpg_jobs command: give Gold Coins or add job XP (Jobs+'s own /job command can only *set*
//     values), and silently grant an advancement (used by the generated Arc actions);
//   - /leavejob: a player drops one of their (at most two) jobs for 5 gold;
//   - job XP for RPG activities that have no Arc action: Apotheosis reforging and salvaging
//     (Smith); Spell Binding Table binds and spell book creation (Enchanter); gem cutting at the
//     Jeweler's Kit and the Apotheosis Gem Cutting Table, Apotheosis socketing and sigils, and
//     Socket Mounts and cut gems set at the anvil (Jeweler); cooking pot meals, keg drinks, food put on a campfire or stove
//     and the first time each dish is made (Cook); the Ossuary and the Mechanical Fusion Anvil (Smith), the cutting
//     board (Cook) and the capture net (Hunter) (pack 1.5.5); the first use of
//     each waystone, each new biome and structure entered, and each map filled in (Explorer);
//   - Survey Maps (Explorer): used up into a map to the nearest place of their kind;
//   - the "extra copy" power-ups: Second Helping (Cook), Mapmaker and Waywright (Explorer);
//   - Hunter skinning: XP for hides, bones and monster parts a Hunter's kills drop, plus extra
//     yield and rare parts by Hunter level;
//   - the reforging gate: reforging to Rare / Epic / Mythic needs Smith 10 / 20 / 30;
//   - class merchants buy job-made goods (emerald income for crafters).
// Job XP only goes to players who have that job (Jobs+ returns no job otherwise), exactly like
// Jobs+'s own job_exp reward.

